  "summary": "The village of Gopalpur in Jajpur District in the Indian state of Odisha is known for producing tussar silk.",
  "description": "The village of Gopalpur in Jajpur District in the Indian state of Odisha is known for producing tussar silk. The handicraft received the Geographical Indication tag by the Government of India in 2009. The fabric may be used for dhoti, shawls, scarves, and saris.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Odisha; registration 2011–12), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
